      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`update_weights_from_disk(recapture_cuda_graph=True)` only recaptures decode graphs. When loading replaces parameter storage, target prefill graphs still replay the old addresses: they can serve stale weights or access freed memory even though the update succeeds.\n\n## Modifications\n\nRoute weight updates through a callback that cleans up and recaptures an existing target prefill graph before recapturing decode, matching startup order. Use a fresh shared pool so prefill-only recapture does not revive a drained pool and hit `CachingHostAllocator`'s `use_count > 0` assertion. Keep the existing speculative draft placement guard; spec-worker-owned draft graph recapture is outside this change. The broader backend cleanup work in #44296 is separate.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nReproduced on H100, PyTorch 2.14.1+cu130, baseline `a99c7d050f`, using Qwen3-0.6B and real HTTP generation/weight-update requests. This is a **controlled parameter-storage reallocation repro**, not a claim that the ordinary Qwen loader reallocates weights:\n\n- Created checkpoint B by negating checkpoint A's MLP down-projection weights. A probe wrapper clones parameter storage before reload and retains the previous storage, making stale reads deterministic.\n- Before the fix, with breakable prefill graphs and decode graphs disabled, all 6 prompts retained A's first token and logprob after updating to B. None matched a fresh eager B server. A second update released the original storage and hit an illegal memory access in prefill.\n- After the fix, tested two consecutive updates with decode graphs disabled and with full decode graphs enabled: all 24 post-update requests matched the fresh eager B server's complete 8-token outputs and token logprobs exactly (maximum difference 0), with no failed requests. Server logs confirm prefill graph replay.\n- Existing draft recapture tests: 3 passed. Ruff lint/format and `git diff --check` passed. No new test files.\n\nGPT-OSS-20B/Marlin was also attempted, but its native reload fails earlier with `default_weight_loader() got an unexpected keyword argument 'weight_name'`; that is not counted as a repro of this issue.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Controlled reproduction setup</summary>\n\nCreate B from a local Qwen3-0.6B checkpoint, retaining its config/tokenizer files:\n\n```python\nfrom safetensors.torch import load_file, save_file\n\nweights = load_file(f\"{checkpoint_a}/model.safetensors\")\nfor name in weights:\n    if name.endswith(\"mlp.down_proj.weight\"):\n        weights[name] = -weights[name]\nsave_file(weights, f\"{checkpoint_b}/model.safetensors\")\n```\n\nInstall this probe in a Python launcher before starting the server (also at module scope so spawned workers install it):\n\n```python\nfrom sglang.srt.models.qwen3 import Qwen3ForCausalLM\n\noriginal_load = Qwen3ForCausalLM.load_weights\n\ndef load(self, weights):\n    if getattr(self, \"_probe_loaded\", False):\n        self._probe_old_weights = [p.data for p in self.parameters()]\n        for p in self.parameters():\n            p.data = p.data.clone()\n    result = original_load(self, weights)\n    self._probe_loaded = True\n    return result\n\nQwen3ForCausalLM.load_weights = load\n```\n\nLaunch A with TP1, `--attention-backend triton --context-length 1024 --max-total-tokens 4096 --chunked-prefill-size 128 --cuda-graph-bs-prefill 4 8 16 32 64 128 --cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable --cuda-graph-backend-decode disabled --disable-overlap-schedule`. For the decode-enabled run, replace the disabled flag with `--cuda-graph-bs-decode 1 2`.\n\nGenerate `The capital of France is` with temperature 0, `max_new_tokens=8`, `ignore_eos=true`, and `return_logprob=true`. POST `/update_weights_from_disk` with `model_path=checkpoint_b`, `load_format=\"auto\"`, and `recapture_cuda_graph=true`, then generate again after flushing the cache. Before the fix the first token/logprob remains `12095 / -0.4147300720214844`; the corrected result and fresh eager B reference are `5015 / -3.8977460861206055`. Repeat the update to exercise graph cleanup and recapture again.\n\n</details>\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nCorrectness fix for explicit weight-update recapture; no inference performance claim.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40200575270](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40200575270)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40200575155](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40200575155)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40200575224](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40200575224)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
